---
import Church from '../layouts/Church.astro';
---
<Church title="Accessibility statement" description="How this site was tested for accessibility, with the results." section="Pages" eyebrow="Everyone is welcome" heading="Accessibility statement" lead="How this site was tested, with the results.">
  <div class="wrap body prose" style="max-width:860px">
    <p>This site aims to meet WCAG 2.2 level AA. It is a concept project and the church is fictional, but the tests below were run on this site.</p>

    <h2>Test results, October 28, 2026</h2>
    <table>
      <caption>Automated and scripted checks, run after the October 28 redesign and the photo update</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Check</th><th scope="col">Result</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">axe-core (WCAG 2.0 and 2.1 A and AA, plus best practices)</th><td>0 violations on 14 pages, at phone and desktop sizes, plus the search page with results and with no results</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Lighthouse accessibility (3 pages: home, sermons, visit, phone profile)</th><td>100 on every page tested</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Lighthouse performance</th><td>95 to 100; the home page is the heaviest because of its photos</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Lighthouse best practices</th><td>100 on every page tested</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Keyboard</th><td>Skip link is the first stop and every stop shows a visible focus ring</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Reflow at 320 and 640 pixels wide</th><td>No horizontal scrolling</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Text spacing</th><td>No clipped text</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Structure</th><td>One h1 per page, no skipped heading levels, every page has a title and description, every image has an alt attribute (empty for decoration)</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Page weight</th><td>About 285 KB or less for any page, including images. The search page loads the search engine when you search, about 190 KB more</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Search</h2>
    <p>Search runs in your browser using Pagefind, with no data sent to a server. The search box and the section menu have labels, the result count is announced to screen readers, and results are a list of links.</p>

    <h2>What was fixed during testing</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The month labels in the date circles were too faint against the dark red. They are now lighter.</li>
      <li>A decorative glow behind the home page headline made the page scroll sideways at 320 pixels wide. It is now clipped.</li>
      <li>Date circles are excluded from search results, so results do not show text like "Nov5".</li>
      <li>Cover pictures for sermons and posts are decorative and hidden from screen readers. The photos on this site are computer-generated for the concept. They are not real people, customers or places.</li>
      <li>The photos were resized to about twice the size they show on screen, which brought the home page performance score back up.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Not yet tested</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Manual screen reader testing (VoiceOver, NVDA), including the search results announcements. This statement will be updated when it is done.</li>
      <li>Lighthouse "SEO" shows 60 to 63, not 100, because the site is deliberately marked <code>noindex</code> so search engines skip this concept project.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Tools: axe-core, Lighthouse 12, Pagefind, and Nest Co.'s own scripted checks.</p>
  </div>
</Church>
